        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T21:21:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why consider all these different cases? Shouldn\u0027t it be:\n\ncase POWER_S0:\n\tlpc_set_host_event_mask(LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE, 0);\n\tbreak;\n\nIn fact I think this entire function can be written a little differently:\n\nstatic void power_set_active_wake_mask(enum power_state state)\n{\n\tuint32_t wake_mask;\n\tuint32_t active_wm \u003d lpc_get_host_event_mask(LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE);\n\n\tif (state \u003d\u003d POWER_S0)\n\t\twake_mask \u003d 0;\n\telse if (active_wm || lpc_get_lazy_wake_mask(state, \u0026wake_mask))\n\t\treturn;\n\n\tlpc_set_host_event_mask(LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE, wake_mask);\n}",
      "range": {
