    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d682367b_ccd451a3",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 237,
      "author": {
        "id": 1130416
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-02T15:17:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With present logic, without having the lazy_wm_in_use check,  active_wm would be set to 0 on S3S5. Even if active wake mask was set by host (before initiating S5), this flow would force use of lazy_wm. But with the new logic suggested by Furquan (previous comment), this would be taken care.",
      "parentUuid": "f8bf287c_59fe35fa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c1d6523163159caae69c9c16773026d31b26a69f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ff0b17d_627aaeb1",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 237,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-02T18:00:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the above logic I provided would cover the case you pointed out. But thinking about it more, I came across two cases that we need to have special handling for:\n\n1. Old BIOS and new EC -- programming of S0ix mask: We need to still use a default S0ix wake mask here if host did not program active mask.\n\n2. New BIOS and new EC -- what happens if host programs both active and lazy masks? -- I have added a paragraph in the design doc towards the end to cover this.\n\nOverall the above logic should look something like this:\nstatic void power_set_active_wake_mask(enum power_state state)\n{\n»       uint32_t wake_mask;\n\n»       /* Reset active mask to 0 after coming back to S0. */\n»       if (state \u003d\u003d POWER_S0)\n»       »       wake_mask \u003d 0;\n»       /* If not in S0, then honor current mask if set by host. */\n»       else if (lpc_is_active_mask_set_by_host())\n»       »       return;\n»       /* If host has not set active mask, check if lazy mask is available. for this power state. */\n»       else if (lpc_get_lazy_wake_mask(state, \u0026wake_mask))\n»       »       return;\n\n»       /* Ensure S0ix mask is non-zero. */\n»       if ((state \u003d\u003d POWER_S0IX) \u0026\u0026 (wake_mask \u003d\u003d 0))\n»       »       wake_mask \u003d get_default_s0ix_mask();\n\n»       /* Set active mask and reset active_mask_set_by_host flag. */\n»       lpc_reset_active_mask(wake_mask);\n}\n\nLet me know what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "d682367b_ccd451a3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c1d6523163159caae69c9c16773026d31b26a69f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59caa43e_4e34ae92",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 237,
      "author": {
        "id": 1214649
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-03T04:36:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see one more corner case \n\nWhen host set lazy wake mask for S3 and S5\n \nWith above logic you suggested , in S5 flow,\n1)System enter S3 : S3 lazy wake mask will be programmed as active wake mask\n2) System enter S3S5: Since active wake mask is set in step 1, power_set_active_wake_mask would return without updating active wake mask\n3)System enter S5: same scenario as step 2 and on S5 system will have S3 active wake mask.\n\nBasically need to find a way to distinguish between active wake mask set by host and active wake mask programmed by  lazy wake mask.",
      "parentUuid": "6ff0b17d_627aaeb1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c1d6523163159caae69c9c16773026d31b26a69f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f315f135_91e6b87e",
        "filename": "power/common.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 237,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-03T04:43:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is the reason I suggested use of lpc_is_active_mask_set_by_host(). \n\n3) In #3 lpc_is_active_mask_set_by_host() will return false. Thus, power_set_active_wake_mask will set the wake mask for POWER_S5 state.\n\nPlease also check the last section in the design doc. It details how to maintain a flag to indicate if the mask is set by host.",
      "parentUuid": "59caa43e_4e34ae92",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
